--TEST--
A literal argument to a constructor carries the name of the constructor parameter it filled, and a literal passed to a callable variable carries no name because the callable type names no parameter
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Person {
    public function constructor(public string $name, public string $city) {}
}
new Person("Ada", "London");
callable(string): void $say = function (string $text): void { echo $text; };
$say("hi");
--REQUEST--
inlayHint
--EXPECT--
5:12 parameter name:
5:19 parameter city:
